close_reason: "A stale session-state lock no longer makes release fail after it wrote: the lease is reclaimed past its TTL, claim and release share one post-commit warning policy, and the stale-lock refusal is typed with a working remedy"
contract_change:
  api: "pm claim and pm release (CLI, SDK runClaim/runRelease, MCP claim/release), stale-lock refusals"
  before: "A stale session-state lock made release clear the claim and exit 4, claim returned a bare attribution warning, and a stale lock kept by policy was refused untyped as an Item lock with a --force hint"
  after: The session-state lease is reclaimed past its TTL; claim and release exit 0 after a committed write and add release_semantic_attribution_unrecorded or claim_semantic_attribution_unrecorded with a suggestion when attribution fails; a kept stale lock is refused with stale_lock_requires_override naming lock_path and pm gc --scope locks
  migrate: "Match stale_lock_requires_override instead of the old message text, and read suggestions beside the attribution warnings; release exit codes need no handling for the session lock"
escape_class: production_defect
